      "Label Studio (D177; owner: \"I need to be able to select from the various size labels, not just rollo but any vendors sizes. I need to be able to switch between 1D and 2D barcodes (qr codes) and the info I want on the label.\"): re-barcode a jar whose barcode is damaged, won't scan or is wrong, or give glass a barcode. Open it from a lot (🏷 Print label), a product page, a received manifest (🏷 Print labels for this manifest), an Other Inventory item, the drafts list or a keyed-in invoice (one label per piece received). Pick the printer and any vendor's label size (Rollo, OnlineLabels, Zebra, DYMO or a custom size the Rollo can feed), choose 1D barcode, 2D QR code or retail UPC, and tick which lines print. The preview is to scale and warns before anything that would not scan. Cannabis labels go beside the producer's label, never over it (WAC 314-55-105). Save a setup as a store design so every device can pick it by name; one design per kind can be the default. Every print is recorded (who, what, how many, which code) and shows under Recent prints. Store designs and print history need database update 0342; printing works without it.",
      "Label printing fixed and calibrated (D191; owner: \"I tested the 2x1 labels, it prints two labels, the first blank, the second nearly prints off the bottom of the label.\"): Chrome rotates a wide page on thermal printers (Chromium issue 372435414), so the studio now sends a 2×1 as a tall 1×2 page with the artwork already turned (Label Studio step 5, Orientation Auto). Each computer can also set Rotate ↻/↺, Nudge in 0.01″ steps and Scale for each label size, and press 🎯 Print test label: if the border is complete and the cross is centred, every label will land right. In the print dialog choose the label's paper size, Margins None and Scale 100%. Set the same custom size once in the Rollo app (Menu → Rollo Printer → Settings → Media). After changing rolls, hold the Rollo's top button until it beeps to recalibrate. Text size Fill (the default) and Edge margin Tight make the text as large as the label allows.",
      "Label printing direction fixed (D196; owner: \"the label maker is still not working right. i have tried all the things.\"): the D191 turned page printed sideways across two labels (QR on one, name on the next), so Orientation Auto now sends every label straight on a page exactly the label's size (a 2×1 is a 2″ × 1″ page). Set this once on the Rollo's own web page (type its IP address into a browser): Media = the label size, Label Separator Gap, and Printing Defaults → Orientation = the upright \"A\" (not \"?\"), then Save. In Chrome's dialog pick the label's paper size, Margins None, Scale Default/100%, then press 🎯 Print test label. Old saved nudges were reset. If it still runs across two labels on Windows, add the printer with Rollo's own driver by TCP/IP (steps in Label Studio step 5). The full product name now wraps onto up to 4 lines next to a QR instead of being cut off with \"…\".",
      "Other Inventory on the register (Phase 4; owner: \"Q-05b-1- yes, and any other upgrade, enhancement and such needed to fully utilize non cannabis goods in the system and on the register and on the menu.\"): every Active item with a price is a register product. Scan its SKU label or its UPC/EAN (a cannabis code always wins a clash) or tap the card. It is taxed 9.3% with no excise and no purchase limit. A completed sale lowers On hand in one database step and books cost of goods at the item's average cost; a void puts the units back once; a counter return either restocks (Put back on the shelf) or is written off, and it is never sent to CCRS. Sale.csv leaves these lines out and says how many. Needs database update 0323.",
      "Other Inventory \u2192 Save change (Phase 4; owner: \"Q-05b-2- owner, admin, manager.\" and \"non cannabis should be allowed to have their cost modified.\"): owner, admin or manager open an item and change its price or cost with a reason. A $0.00 price is refused, the SKU never changes, and the audit log keeps old \u2192 new. If someone else changed it first, the save is refused so nothing is overwritten.",
      "Other Inventory \u2192 controls (Phase 4; owner: \"Q-05b-5- yes, plan on the group of smaller fixes.\"): Confirm and Archive are audited and an archived item can be Restored (it comes back as a draft, same SKU). Adjustments are one atomic step that never go below zero; the direction is set by the reason (only Count correction and Other let you pick). Recent adjustments shows who (By) and Pacific time. A paper invoice saves all-or-nothing and updates each item's cost to the weighted average. The page shows Register sales \u2014 last 30 days (units, sales, cost, margin per item).",
