      "Set up our daily deals (owner rule D134, 2026-11-02): on Promotions, the Set up our daily deals panel compares Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Friday, Saturday and Sunday with the standard week (Monday 25% edibles, tinctures and RSO; Tuesday prerolls 1+ items 20%, 4+ items 25%; Wednesday concentrates, carts and RSO 20%, 30% at $150+; Friday flower 7g 15%, 14g 20%, 28g 30%; Saturday 30% off one item and 15% off the rest; Sunday buy 3 pay for 2) and lists every change. Pressing the button saves and publishes each day through the same pre-publish check as Publish; a day that fails the check is skipped and named. Your titles, descriptions, bonus notes and product or brand exclusions are kept. Thursday is never touched: it is set up by hand each week (Guided Thursday setup or the Thursday planner). Pressing it again when everything matches changes nothing.",
      "Which sections do I need? (owner rule D136): every promotion form has a Which sections do I need? table. For each kind of deal it says which boxes to fill and which are ignored. Steps marked (always) are needed on every promotion; (optional) steps can be left alone. Every field has an \u24d8 hint: hover or tap it. An either/or deal gives the customer the better of the two options.",
      "Wording heads-up (owner rule D135): while you type a promotion's title, description or bonus note, a gold box warns about wording Washington does not allow in cannabis ads (free or giveaway, anything aimed at minors, health or safety claims, encouraging over-use, alcohol or tobacco references such as happy hour, best or lowest price claims, vendor-paid wording, unlimited) and about text that does not match the deal (a percent, dollar amount, bundle, weekday, product type, brand or storewide claim the deal does not give). Each one says why and suggests wording. It never stops a save or a publish; the promotions list shows a wording heads-up count. It is a professional check, not legal advice.",
      "Deals on the register are always today's (owner rule D133): each deal on the register knows its weekday. The register checks every 30 seconds; when the day changes it drops yesterday's deals at once, says Today's deals are not loaded on this register yet, and loads today's on its own (or press Refresh menu in the More menu). Each sale records which day's deals it used, and the office audit log gets register.promo_day_mismatch if a synced sale used deals that were not live at the time (the sale is never refused).",
