      "Money & accounting: Accounting settings (GL mapping + Sage 50 export) and AI usage & cost.",
      "Equipment & integrations: Equipment (hardware hub), Receipt printer, and Integrations (Leafly/WeedMaps).",
      "Team & security: Users & roles, Activity log, and Security & passkeys (Face ID / Touch ID sign-in).",
      "Data & lifecycle: Reset operational data — clears test sales/inventory/imports/customers before going live, while keeping your settings and knowledge base.",
      "Admin \u2192 Platform health (G-71a, owner message 12): every morning at about 6:25am Pacific the system asks the database whether the server can still read and call every table and function the app uses (the list is rebuilt from the code). Staff get one email a day: All clear, Warning or ACTION NEEDED with the exact fix, usually a migration to run in the Supabase SQL editor. Phones get a push only when something is wrong. Run check now records a run without emailing. This is the check that would have caught the October 30, 2026 Supabase change that broke customer returns. It needs migration 0331_platform_health.sql; until then the page says to run it.",
      "Admin \u2192 Platform health also shows the platform changes register (G-71b, owner message 12): upcoming Supabase, Vercel, Next.js, GitHub and Node.js changes that could affect Greenway, each with its deadline, what it means for us and what to do. Staff get a monthly review email at the start of each month and a warning 30, 7 and 1 day before each open deadline, and once if it is overdue. The register is updated at each monthly review (standing rule 16); the page flags it if no review has happened in 45 days. No migration is needed.",
      "Platform health also runs a daily money-path test (G-71c, owner message 12): every morning the server opens a test till, rings up a test sale, takes it out of stock, writes it to the books as a draft, takes a customer return, drops cash and closes the till, then undoes all of it inside the database, so nothing is left behind. If a step fails, the morning email names the step, what it breaks at the counter (for example customer returns) and the fix. It needs migration 0332_money_path_smoke_test.sql; until then Platform health shows a warning that the test is not installed.",
      "Platform health also watches for errors all day (G-71d, owner message 12): when a page or action crashes, or the database refuses the server (\"permission denied\", or a table or function the app needs is missing), it is recorded under Recent errors on Admin \u2192 Platform health. Staff are emailed and pushed straight away on the first permission refusal, the third missing table or function, or five crashes within 10 minutes, at most once per kind per hour. The morning email adds the last 24 hours. Messages are saved without tokens, emails or long numbers. It needs migration 0333_platform_error_events.sql; until then the page says error alerting is not installed.",
      "Locked versions (G-71e, owner message 14: \"Please now complete item 5 to close all gaps. Fit inside this slice the node.js fixes too please.\"): every library the website and the merch site use is locked to one exact version, so nothing changes by itself. New versions are found by an upgrade check run at the monthly platform review (G-74, owner message 16: \"Can we go back to the old way of merging pr\u2019s?\"): small updates go in one Greenway Dev pull request, each big (major) update in its own, and every one must pass every automatic check, including a full site build, before it is merged (standing rule 17). Dependabot is switched off, so no bot pull requests arrive any more. The website, its checks and production all run Node.js 24, set in the code rather than the Vercel dashboard; Node.js 20, which Supabase and Vercel no longer support, is gone. No migration is needed.",
